1.You must walk at your own speed: Don’t try to walk hard, as this will consume a lot of energy. If you are hiking with a lot of people, it is best to find a companion who is about the same speed as you.
Measure your physical fitness scientifically: It is best to stick to walking for a few hours during the first few hikes, rather than plan how far you must go. After you have learned about your own abilities through such a few surveys, Appropriately increase the intensity of trekking.
Don’t just walk with your head down and miss the surrounding scenery: walking outdoors, keeping fit is only one of the purposes. Don’t go violently for some so-called “self-masturbation” purposes.
Learn to rest footwork: Everyone has their own way of walking. When hiking, you should use a more comfortable way to walk, so that your physical strength can be used scientifically and effectively.
Pay attention to rest scientifically during the hike: Generally, you need to rest for 10 minutes every 50 minutes of walking. Different people can measure the addition or subtraction according to their own situation.
