The infrared transmittance is very high (up to 80%), and the thermal insulation performance is poor. In the sunny and windless early spring night, the phenomenon of “temperature inversion” may occur in the greenhouse and freeze damage crops.
Poor strength, poor resilience and easy to tear.
Advantages of polyvinyl chloride film (PVC): colorless and transparent, high strength, tensile strength up to 27.5mpa. The infrared transmittance is small (20%), it has good thermal insulation, acid, alkali and salt resistance, and it is not easy to deteriorate when sprayed with pesticides and fertilizers.
The purpose of longevity can be achieved only by selecting the repackaged resin with melt flow rate MFR = 0.3 ~ 0.8 and high-efficiency hindered amine light stabilizer. For PVC long-life membrane, when UV absorber is selected, it has a strong protective effect on the membrane.
Colored film: visible light with a wavelength of 400 ~ 700 nm plays a leading role in photosynthesis in solar light, which is called photosynthetic effective radiation. Among them, blue violet light with a wavelength of 400 ~ 510 nm and red orange light with a wavelength of 610 ~ 720 nm have the greatest impact on Photosynthesis and green light has the least.
Aging resistance. It is the film with the longest service life at present, and can be covered continuously for 15 ~ 20 years.
Disadvantages: large glass ratio (2500kg / m3), strict requirements for greenhouse foundation and framework, and high initial cost, maintenance cost, operation cost and depreciation cost; Low impact resistance and fragile; Poor thermal insulation performance. At present, many large cities have discouraged the construction of glass greenhouses.
Polycarbonate sheet (PC) is one of the most advanced polymers in plastic applications. 1.
It has good dimensional stability and good heat resistance, and can be used for a long time at – 60 ~ 120 ℃. The thermal deformation temperature is greater than 310 ℃, and the flammability specification belongs to self extinguishing resin, with small polarity, low water absorption, light stability and good weather resistance.
The thermal insulation performance is extremely high, and its heat transfer coefficient can be reduced to 1.6 ~ 2.2w/m2 ℃, which is 30% ~ 60% more energy-saving than that of glass greenhouse. There are three types: flat plate, wave plate and multilayer hollow plate.
