What is the function of “g” end of instrument?
The “g” end of the instrument is to bypass the leakage current on the surface of the tested object, so that the leakage current does not pass through the test circuit of the instrument, eliminating the error caused by the leakage current. When testing the high resistance value, the G end needs to be used.
