The copper clad steel wire is a bimetallic wire with a steel wire as its core and a copper layer on the outside. The copper clad steel wire combines the mechanical properties of high tensile strength of steel, high electrical properties of copper conductivity and low contact resistance in performance, so it has the characteristics of high conduction efficiency and high tensile strength.
(2) Under the same cross-section and condition, the mechanical strength of copper clad steel wire is twice that of solid copper wire. It can withstand large impacts and loads.
The copper clad steel wire we provided can meet the requirements of ASTM B869, ASTM B452 and other standards. The tensile strength can be produced with high-quality steel such as low carbon steel, medium carbon steel and high carbon steel according to customers' needs.
Application The copper clad steel wire can be used as the inner conductor of the coaxial cable of the cable TV subscriber line; Can be used as the overhead line of power transmission and telephone lines; Can be used as the lead wire and antenna of various electronic devices in the electronics industry.
