Geology and mining: demand recovery
At present, China is still in the middle stage of industrialization, and the growth rate of energy resource demand is slowing down, but the total demand will remain high. It is estimated that by 2020, China’s primary energy consumption will be about 5 billion tons of standard coal, 750 million tons of iron ore, 13.5 million tons of refined copper and 35 million tons of original aluminum.
In the next two years, as the prices of coal, oil and metal minerals remain high, it is expected that the mining and exploration willingness will continue to rise, and the demand for cemented carbide for geological and mining tools will continue to increase significantly. It is expected that the demand growth rate will be maintained at about 20% in 2018-2019.
Wear resistant cemented carbide is mainly used in mechanical structure products of various wear-resistant fields, including molds, high-pressure and high-temperature cavity, wear-resistant parts, etc. At present, the cemented carbide used for various molds accounts for about 8% of the total output of cemented carbide, and the cavity for high pressure and high temperature resistance accounts for about 9% of the total output of cemented carbide.
It is estimated that the composite growth rate of die cemented carbide demand in 2017-2019 will be about 9%. In addition, the demand for cemented carbide for high-pressure and high-temperature resistant cavities and wear-resistant mechanical parts is expected to increase by 14.65% and 14.79% respectively in 2018-2019, and the demand will reach 11024 tons and 12654 tons.
